# the app, not meant to be a permanent repo artifact
debug/

# scripts/buildCityBoundaries.mjs's US output (public/geo/city-boundaries/840/)
# is a reshaped duplicate of already-committed public/geo/us-cities/*.json
# (47 MB) - no network round-trip needed to regenerate it (unlike Jordan/
# Kuwait's, which cost real Overpass/geoBoundaries calls and ARE committed),
# so committing a second ~50 MB copy of the same underlying data would just
# double repo size for nothing. Regenerate with `npm run build:geo:city-boundaries`.
public/geo/city-boundaries/840/
